  data: {
    LLM: '1. Deal one card at a time into a row of face-up piles. 2. A top card may move onto the pile immediately to its left or three piles to its left if the destination top card matches suit or rank. 3. After a move, close gaps so piles stay contiguous. 4. Continue moving whenever legal moves exist. 5. Hand ends when no legal moves remain.',
    Player: '1. Deal one card at a time into a row of face-up piles. 2. A top card may move onto the pile immediately to its left or three piles to its left if the destination top card matches suit or rank. 3. After a move, close gaps so piles stay contiguous. 4. Continue moving whenever legal moves exist. 5. Hand ends when no legal moves remain.',
    objective: 'Compress the entire deck into a single pile. The game is won when all 52 cards are in one pile; the layout is so named because compressing the row resembles closing accordion pleats.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal one card at a time into a row of face-up piles. 2. A top card may move onto the pile immediately to its left or three piles to its left if the destination top card matches suit or rank. 3. After a move, close gaps so piles stay contiguous. 4. Continue moving whenever legal moves exist. 5. Hand ends when no legal moves remain.',
    keyRules: [
      'Moves are always to the left.',
      'A move is legal only when suit or rank matches the destination top card.',
      'The allowed jump distances are exactly 1-left and 3-left.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'One player. Accordion is a patience (solitaire) game played by a single player; there are no opponents or partners.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
      equipment: 'One shuffled deck and table space for a long row of piles.',
      dealing: 'Deal cards one by one from stock into a single row. After each deal, resolve any legal compression moves before dealing again if playing the incremental style.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Deal one card at a time into a row of face-up piles. 2. A top card may move onto the pile immediately to its left or three piles to its left if the destination top card matches suit or rank. 3. After a move, close gaps so piles stay contiguous. 4. Continue moving whenever legal moves exist. 5. Hand ends when no legal moves remain.',
