    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Compress the entire deck into a single pile. The game is won when all 52 cards are in one pile; the layout is so named because compressing the row resembles closing accordion pleats.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Deal one card at a time into a row of face-up piles. 2. A top card may move onto the pile immediately to its left or three piles to its left if the destination top card matches suit or rank. 3. After a move, close gaps so piles stay contiguous. 4. Continue moving whenever legal moves exist. 5. Hand ends when no legal moves remain.',
      'Scoring example: Score by final number of piles; fewer is better. Finish with exactly one pile..',
